Is there any point for healers in #enhance'ing healing spells? - It's the
healer's single spell class, which they start at Basic proficiency, and
all interesting (level 1-3) spells, from healing to cure sickness, can be
reliably casted when necessary. The only exception is the (even somewhat
useless) level 4 spell of restore ability.

I would see a point in enhancing the healing spell if the healing grade
(i.e. the amount of restored HP's) would depend on the proficiency, but
that seems not be the case.

Even for other classes it seems unnecessary to enchance that spell class.
Once extra healing can be casted it's not worth any more to cast it; two
separate healing casts are cheaper (WRT Pw) and typically you have the
time to cast but have not enough Pw to waste.

